        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: событие",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "событие (sobýtiye) — \"an event\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Это было важное событие для всей семьи. Éto býlo vázhnoye sobýtiye dlya vsey semí. It was an important event for the whole family."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. Место событий — the scene."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "событие (sobýtiye) is built on со- \"together\" and бытие \"being\", from быть \"to be\", inherited from Proto-Slavic byti, from PIE bʰuH- (EtymDB): what came to be."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
